+# Narrowing Veterinarian Search to Allow Filtering
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. The row was derived from observed absence, and its wording covered any way of narrowing the veterinarian directory. A request to filter the directory by specialty fell inside that wording.
+
+The owner decided the row on 2026-10-30, quoted from the slice's intake record:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+The same intake bounds the filter:
+
+> The filter is a URL contract only. Neither surface gains a form, dropdown, or other page control in this request; pagination links carry the parameter so filtered pages stay navigable. A visible control may come as a follow-up request.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 as written.** Rejected by the owner's decision above.
+2. **Remove NG-9.** Rejected: free-text veterinarian search stays out, and the decision does not touch pet or visit search.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 and record the page control as declined for now** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Free-text veterinarian search, pet search, and visit search stay out of scope. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope. The specialty filter is the first such filter.
+
+A page control for the filter is out of scope, recorded as NG-10. NG-10 is a deferral: a follow-up request may reopen it on an owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 and NG-10 leave the open provenance consultation; the Non-Goals preamble names them decided.
+- The specialty filter exists only in the URL, so a reader finds it through a link or by typing the address.
+- A veterinarian's name is an attribute the directory shows. Whether filtering on it falls within this narrowing stays an open question in the PRD.
+- Any filter beyond specialty needs its own request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the added row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement this narrowing admits.
