+# Query-Side Case Folding for the Specialty Filter
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` requires a specialty name to match disregarding letter case on every supported database. The three schemas disagree on case. `specialties.name` is case-sensitive under H2 and PostgreSQL, and follows the database collation under MySQL. Owner search relies on the column type, and the PostgreSQL schema does not provide it, which is a recorded defect of `REQ-OWN-002`.
+
+The schemas are script-managed with no migration tool, so a column change reaches only a freshly initialized database.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Column types per vendor** - `VARCHAR_IGNORECASE` under H2, a case-insensitive type under PostgreSQL. Rejected: it edits three scripts, misses populated databases, and repeats the route that produced the owner-search defect.
+2. **Fetch the veterinarians and compare in Java** - Rejected: paging and page counts would be recomputed in the controller, away from the query.
+3. **Fold both operands in the query expression** (chosen) - One JPQL predicate, identical on all three vendors.
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty filter lower-cases both the stored name and the parameter inside the repository query. No vendor schema changes for this filter. A later filter on a text attribute follows the same form.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- One predicate behaves the same on H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL for letter case, and it needs no schema edit.
+- The predicate cannot use the plain index on `specialties.name`. The Specialties row in § Scale and Load treats that table as bounded.
+- MySQL still applies the column collation to the folded comparison. A pad-space collation treats trailing spaces as equal, and an accent-insensitive one ignores accents.
+- The H2-backed suite cannot show vendor behavior, so the PostgreSQL and MySQL integration tests exercise the match.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Persistence](../system-design.md#persistence)
+- [Script-Managed Schema Across Three Database Vendors](2026-07-31-script-managed-multi-vendor-schema.md)
